{"entities":"[{\"text\": \"Ethacrynic acid\", \"id\": \"D004976\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"convulsions\", \"id\": \"D012640\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"ethacrynic acid\", \"id\": \"D004976\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"convulsive\", \"id\": \"D012640\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"5-hydroxytryptamine\", \"id\": \"D012701\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"5-HT\", \"id\": \"D012701\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"gamma-aminobutyric acid\", \"id\": \"D005680\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"acetylcholine\", \"id\": \"D000109\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"glutamate\", \"id\": \"D018698\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"N-methyl-D-aspartate\", \"id\": \"D016202\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"aminophosphonovaleric acid\", \"id\": \"-1\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"ethacrynic acid\", \"id\": \"D004976\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"convulsions\", \"id\": \"D012640\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}]","filtered_entities":[{"text":"Ethacrynic acid","id":"D004976","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"convulsions","id":"D012640","label":"Disease"},{"text":"5-hydroxytryptamine","id":"D012701","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"gamma-aminobutyric acid","id":"D005680","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"acetylcholine","id":"D000109","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"glutamate","id":"D018698","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"N-methyl-D-aspartate","id":"D016202","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"aminophosphonovaleric acid","id":"-1","label":"Chemical"}],"head":"aminophosphonovaleric acid","head_id":"-1","pairs":[{"head":"Ethacrynic acid","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"D004976","tail_id":"D012640"},{"head":"5-hydroxytryptamine","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"D012701","tail_id":"D012640"},{"head":"gamma-aminobutyric acid","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"D005680","tail_id":"D012640"},{"head":"acetylcholine","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"D000109","tail_id":"D012640"},{"head":"glutamate","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"D018698","tail_id":"D012640"},{"head":"N-methyl-D-aspartate","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"D016202","tail_id":"D012640"},{"head":"aminophosphonovaleric acid","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"-1","tail_id":"D012640"}],"relations":["D004976 | D012640"],"result":"~","tail":"convulsions","tail_id":"D012640","text":"Ethacrynic acid-induced convulsions and brain neurotransmitters in mice. Intracerebroventricular injection of ethacrynic acid (50% convulsive dose; 50 micrograms/mouse) accelerated the synthesis/turnover of 5-hydroxytryptamine (5-HT) but suppressed the synthesis of gamma-aminobutyric acid and acetylcholine in mouse brain. These effects were completely antagonized by pretreatment with a glutamate/N-methyl-D-aspartate antagonist, aminophosphonovaleric acid. In ethacrynic acid-induced convulsions, these neurotransmitter systems may be differentially modulated, probably through activation of glutaminergic neurons in the brain.","metrics":{"precision":1.0,"recall":1.0,"f1":1.0,"rel_tp":1,"rel_fp":0,"rel_fn":0}}